rriculum and Requirements\nCourse Descriptions\nLab Rotations\nMentorship\nOpen DrawerClose Drawer\nSelecting a Mentor\nAvailable Mentors\nMentoring and Training Agreement\nStudent Commitments\nMentor Commitments\nFinancial Support\nProgram Contacts\nReady to Apply?\nApplication Instructions\nTuition and Financial Support\nAll full-time Ph.D. students in the Biomedical Sciences receive the following:\nFull tuition support (student activity fees are paid by the student)\nAnnual stipend is $46,000 for the 2024-2025 academic year\nHealth insurance is covered at 100%; students are responsible for enrollment\nStudent Accounts\nThe most recent student fee information is available from the Office of Student Accounts.\nView Student Fees\nView Student Account in Canelink\nOffice of Financial Assistance\nFinancial aid is available through federal and private loans for students who need additional financial support. Applicants will automatically be considered for a limited number of scholarships. Both federal and private educational loans require students to complete the Free Application for Federal Student Aid. The FAFSA helps lenders determine a student\u2019s eligibility for aid and the amount of aid needed. State and institutional aid sources also require a completed FAFSA. Please refer to the link below for further loan information (including loan opportunities for international students).\nGraduate Professional Financial Assistance\nHealth Insurance\nGraduate students enrolled full-time at the University of Miami are required to obtain adequate health insurance. The university offers a student health insurance plan through the student health service.\nU.S. citizens and permanent residents with adequate health insurance may request to waive the insurance fee via CaneLink.\nStudent Health\nInstagram\nTwitter\nfacebook\nResearch Gate\nLinkedIn\nTikTok\nThreads - UMiami Medicine\nYou tube\nResources\nCareers\nNews\nFor Media\nResearch\nMyUM\nUM Network\nAlumni Association\nG